=== Files ===
[https://petscan.wmflabs.org/?categories=Memory+of+the+World+Register&wikidata_label_language=&referrer_url=&outlinks_yes=&ores_prob_to=&page_image=any&sortby=none&cb_labels_yes_l=1&language=commons&labels_no=&show_soft_redirects=no&links_to_no=&edits%5Bflagged%5D=both&ores_type=any&max_sitelink_count=&cb_labels_any_l=1&show_redirects=no&search_wiki=&outlinks_no=&rxp_filter=&cb_labels_no_l=1&depth=6&langs_labels_no=&manual_list=&search_max_results=500&edits%5Bbots%5D=both&minlinks=&namespace_conversion=keep&search_filter=&negcats=&before=&interface_language=en&sitelinks_no=&project=wikimedia&after=&links_to_any=&wpiu=any&maxlinks=&ns%5B6%5D=1&edits%5Banons%5D=both&min_redlink_count=1&ores_prediction=any Petscan] finds 39,086 files on Commons in the category [[:commons:Category:Memory of the World Register|Memory of the World Register]], with a depth of 6 (larger depths don't give a result; the tool times out). It's difficult to tell how many of these are images are directly of objects that are part of a MotW inscription: a lot seem to be only tangentially related.

GLAMorgan reports 247,169,844 image views for these images in January 2024. However, a lot of these image views are from flags and emblems such as [[:commons:Flag of Queensland.svg]], so the category seems insufficiently precise.

Which of these images have Featured Image awards or other quality badges? Which have been featured on the front page of Wikipedias? We can't tell until the categorisation is much better.

